abstract: "For each of the 50 US states and the District of Columbia, how far Medicaid estate recovery reaches (probate estate only, or beyond it) and whether recovery can reach a house passing at death by a traditional life estate, a lady bird (enhanced life estate) deed, a transfer on death deed, joint tenancy or a revocable living trust. Also records transfer on death deed statutes with effective dates and lady bird deed recognition by authority. Every classification cites the governing statute, regulation, Medicaid manual or State Plan text, with saved copies of each source."
keywords:
  - Medicaid
  - estate recovery
  - lady bird deed
  - transfer on death deed
  - life estate
  - elder law
  - estate planning
  - United States
